WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.517
Easy Science. Why Do We Have Day and Night?

00:00:03.517 --> 00:00:08.149
Every morning the sun comes up, and every evening it goes down.

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:10.972
It looks as if the sun moves around the earth.

00:00:10.972 --> 00:00:13.426
But that is not what really happens.

00:00:13.426 --> 00:00:19.395
The earth is a huge ball, and it turns all the time, like a ball turning on a finger.

00:00:19.395 --> 00:00:22.658
It turns around once every twenty-four hours.

00:00:22.658 --> 00:00:28.080
The sun shines on the earth, but it can only light one half of the ball at a time.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.300
On the side that faces the sun, it is day.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.685
On the other side, it is night.

00:00:33.685 --> 00:00:39.007
As the earth turns, your town moves slowly out of the light and into the dark.

00:00:39.007 --> 00:00:40.273
That is evening.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:43.337
Hours later, it moves back into the light.

00:00:43.337 --> 00:00:44.573
That is morning.

00:00:44.573 --> 00:00:50.515
So when you are eating breakfast, people on the other side of the world are getting ready for bed.

00:00:50.515 --> 00:00:55.517
We do not feel the earth turning, because everything around us turns with it.

00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:57.856
But it is moving very fast.

00:00:57.856 --> 00:01:04.286
Near the middle of the earth, the ground moves at more than one thousand six hundred kilometers an hour.
